printed":"Total"},{"arm_id":"A10","value_printed":"49.6","cell":"C34","col":8,"prose":null,"value_occurrence":null,"variance":{"kind":"none","value_printed":"","n_runs":null},"column_printed":"Total"},{"arm_id":"A11","value_printed":"42.2","cell":"C35","col":8,"prose":null,"value_occurrence":null,"variance":{"kind":"none","value_printed":"","n_runs":null},"column_printed":"Total"}]}],"evidence":[{"id":"E01","cond":"S03","quote":"We present Seed Diffusion Preview, a large-scale language model based on discrete-state diffusion, offering remarkably fast inference speed.","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E02","cond":"S04","quote":"Seed Diffusion Preview is a discrete-state diffusion language model trained with two types of forward corruption process","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E03","cond":"D01","quote":"For the first 80% diffusion training steps, we use a standard mask-based corruption process [12, 15]","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E04","cond":"D01","quote":"For the last 20% diffusion training steps, we add an extra edit-based corruption process as augmentation to improve calibration","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E05","cond":"D01","quote":"The forward process then samples a corrupted sequence based on a predefined edit operation set (e.g., deletions, insertions, and substitutions)","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E06","cond":"D02","quote":"The corrupted sequence xt is sampled from the conditional distribution q(xt|x0) where each token is treated independently","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E07","cond":"D04","quote":"We set the predicted probability over the mask token always as 0 [12]","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E08","cond":"D07.blockwise","quote":"we employ a block-level parallel diffusion sampling scheme that maintains a causal ordering between blocks","loc":"p.5, §3.4"},{"id":"E09","cond":"D10","quote":"Such a model learns a spurious correlation that unmasked tokens are always correct, leading to overconfidence and unable to perform self-correction during inference. To mitigate this, our edit-based augmentation forces the model to re-evaluate all tokens, including those unmasked.","loc":"p.4, §3.1"},{"id":"E10","cond":"D11","quote":"We use KV-caching for previously generated blocks to condition subsequent ones.","loc":"p.5, §3.4"},{"id":"E11","cond":"D11","quote":"Although this risks potentially introducing potential bias, we empirically observe no significant degradation in generation quality.","loc":"p.5, §3.4"},{"id":"E12","cond":"D15","quote":"Our learning objective derives from ELBO in Eq. 6 by substituting the reconstruct loss with a denoised loss based on the edit-based forward process qedit as:","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E13","cond":"S09","quote":"The first stage is scaled diffusion training.","loc":"p.3, §3.1"},{"id":"E14","cond":"S09","quote":"This procedure involves creating a distilled dataset of optimal generation trajectories.","loc":"p.4, §3.2"},{"id":"E15","cond":"S09","quote":"we propose a simple yet effective on-policy learning paradigm","loc":"p.4, §3.3"},{"id":"E16","cond":"S09","quote":"thus adopting the data pipelines (code/code-related data only) and processing methodology of the open-sourced Seed Coder project [20]","loc":"p.2, §3"},{"id":"E17","cond":"S13","quote":"we introduce Seed Diffusion Preview, a code-focused language model designed to achieve an elegant balance between speed and quality","loc":"p.2, §1"},{"id":"E18","cond":"S15","quote":"Direct comparison with baselines is challenging due to differing test conditions: Mercury Coder was evaluated on a proprietary dataset with H100s","loc":"p.1, §Figure 1"},{"id":"E19","cond":"I1","quote":"As shown in Tables 1, 2, 3 and Fig. 1, our model not only achieves performance comparable to advanced autoregressive models while operating at significantly higher speeds, but also delivers a notable boost on editing tasks.","loc":"p.8, §4.2"},{"id":"E20","cond":"I3","quote":"The impact on performance across different block sizes is detailed in Figure 2b.","loc":"p.6, §3.4"},{"id":"E21","cond":"H01","quote":"Seed Diffusion Preview achieves an inference speed of 2,146 token/s over H20 GPUs while maintaining competitive performance across a sweep of standard code evaluation benchmarks","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E22","cond":"CL1","quote":"Seed Diffusion Preview achieves an inference speed of 2,146 token/s over H20 GPUs while maintaining competitive performance across a sweep of standard code evaluation benchmarks","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E23","cond":"CL1","quote":"significantly faster than contemporary Mercury and Gemini, establishing new state of the art on the speed-quality Pareto frontier for code models.","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E24","cond":"CL1","quote":"our model achieves a remarkable speed of 2146 tokens/second on H20 GPUs","loc":"p.2, §1"},{"id":"E25","cond":"CT2","quote":"Seed Diffusion Preview achieves an inference speed of 2,146 token/s over H20 GPUs while maintaining competitive performance across a sweep of standard code evaluation benchmarks","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E26","cond":"QA3d","quote":"Seed Diffusion Preview achieves an inference speed of 2,146 token/s over H20 GPUs while maintaining competitive performance across a sweep of standard code evaluation benchmarks","loc":"p.1, abstract"},{"id":"E27","cond":"G01","quote":"As shown in Tables 1, 2, 3 and Fig. 1, our model not only achieves performance comparable to advanced autoregressive models while operating at significantly higher speeds, but also delivers a notable boost on editing tasks.","loc":"p.8, §4.2"},{"id":"E28","cond":"G02","quote":"As shown in Tables 1, 2, 3 and Fig. 1, our model not only achieves performance comparable to advanced autoregressive models while operating at significantly higher speeds, but also delivers a notable boost on editing tasks.","loc":"p.8, §4.2"},{"id":"E29","cond":"G03","quote":"As shown in Tables 1, 2, 3 and Fig. 1, our model not only achieves performance comparable to advanced autoregressive models while operating at 